diff --git a/omnigent/spec/AGENTSPEC.md b/omnigent/spec/AGENTSPEC.md
index 8ccf45e1b..986882d57 100644
--- a/omnigent/spec/AGENTSPEC.md
+++ b/omnigent/spec/AGENTSPEC.md
@@ -71,6 +71,52 @@ params:                       # arbitrary key-value; readable by skills and tool
   prefer_recent: true
 ```
 
+### `executor.fallbacks` — ordered native model backups
+
+Native Codex and Claude executors can declare up to two explicit backups:
+
+```yaml
+executor:
+  type: omnigent
+  model: gpt-6-astra
+  reasoning_effort: xhigh
+  config:
+    harness: codex-native
+    yolo: false
+  fallbacks:
+    - model: claude-fable-5-1
+      harness: claude-native
+      reasoning_effort: max
+    - model: claude-opus-5
+      harness: claude-native
+      reasoning_effort: max
+```
+
+The default is an empty list, so existing agents do not gain automatic model
+switching. Each entry accepts only `model`, `harness`, and optional
+`reasoning_effort`. Both the primary and backups must use `codex-native` or
+`claude-native`, with an explicit primary model. Duplicate model/harness pairs,
+unsupported effort values, and more than two backups are rejected. Chains use
+host-managed native credentials; executor auth, connection, and profile
+overrides are not supported. Model availability still requires host verification.
+
+Recovery applies to a runner-captured, persisted console/API input whose native
+failure identifies the same attempt and proves that no model work occurred.
+Eligible failures are model unavailability, rate limits, and provider
+unavailability. Authentication, permission denials, cancellation, unknown
+failures, and failures after output or tool work do not authorize replay. Direct
+typing in a native terminal without a captured input is outside this contract.
+Startup errors without equivalent proof must remain failures rather than being
+treated as safe replay automatically.
+
+The replacement keeps the original role, instructions, tools, skills, and policy
+binding. History reconstruction excludes the captured input, which is then sent
+once to the replacement. Cross-provider launch permissions remain conservative.
+Report the model actually used after a fallback; configured role names are not
+execution evidence. Two roles that finish on the same model family do not
+establish cross-model review. This is runtime configuration, not a prompt-only
+retry instruction or a guarantee that a provider will become available.
+
 ### `interaction` axes
 
 | Field | What it means | Who acts on it |
